WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.308 --> 00:00:04.322
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:04.322 --> 00:00:06.204
I started the Mentor
Me series with the goal

00:00:06.204 --> 00:00:08.696
to hang around people who've
done a lot more than us

00:00:08.696 --> 00:00:10.523
and hopefully some of their mindsets,

00:00:10.523 --> 00:00:13.386
way of thinking, values seep into us

00:00:13.386 --> 00:00:16.896
to help us become the
best version of ourselves.

00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:20.223
So today we've compiled a
list of all of the best clips

00:00:20.223 --> 00:00:22.831
from Gary Vaynerchuk in 2016

00:00:22.831 --> 00:00:24.516
of his best motivation

00:00:24.516 --> 00:00:27.927
to help you get ready for an amazing 2017.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.492
And as always, as Gary's talking,

00:00:29.492 --> 00:00:31.542
if he says something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:31.542 --> 00:00:33.161
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:33.161 --> 00:00:34.179
and put quotes around it

00:00:34.179 --> 00:00:36.537
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:37.370
Enjoy.

00:00:38.507 --> 00:00:41.340
(uplifting music)

00:00:51.682 --> 00:00:52.515
- [Gary] It breaks my heart.

00:00:52.515 --> 00:00:55.104
My friends, like, live for Friday night.

00:00:55.104 --> 00:00:56.132
Like they know they get the,

00:00:56.132 --> 00:00:57.811
like Monday morning is the worst.

00:00:57.811 --> 00:01:00.476
It's just such a huge
percentage of one's life

00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:02.482
I can't wrap my head
around what the internet,

00:01:02.482 --> 00:01:04.659
this is not your grandpappy's life.

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:07.014
We have the internet.

00:01:07.014 --> 00:01:09.733
You can build businesses or side hustles.

00:01:09.733 --> 00:01:12.512
I just don't understand
why people relegate

00:01:12.512 --> 00:01:15.023
into losing mentality and
just thinking they can't.

00:01:15.023 --> 00:01:17.038
You can't because you want
to be on the bowling team

00:01:17.038 --> 00:01:18.468
or softball, or play video games,

00:01:18.468 --> 00:01:19.548
that's why you can't.

00:01:19.548 --> 00:01:21.347
There's plenty of time, get shit done.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.871
The level of complaining is unacceptable.

00:01:23.871 --> 00:01:26.029
Look, what if I told you

00:01:26.029 --> 00:01:28.448
this was the last Monday
morning of your life.

00:01:28.448 --> 00:01:30.000
What if I told you you'd die this week.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.273
Would you complain about your crap job?

00:01:32.273 --> 00:01:33.902
Or that test you don't want to take?

00:01:33.902 --> 00:01:34.836
I doubt it.

00:01:34.836 --> 00:01:37.411
You would go much higher level thinking.

00:01:37.411 --> 00:01:38.858
Well, that's really what it takes.

00:01:38.858 --> 00:01:42.539
It takes understanding that if
you're not pumped right now,

00:01:42.539 --> 00:01:44.788
if you're begrudging
what you're about to do,

00:01:44.788 --> 00:01:46.463
if you're not looking forward,

00:01:46.463 --> 00:01:48.990
please recognize the
world we're living in.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:49.823
We're living in a world

00:01:49.823 --> 00:01:51.448
where there's so much more opportunity.

00:01:51.448 --> 00:01:54.308
This internet thing created
way more opportunity

00:01:54.308 --> 00:01:55.345
for all of us.

00:01:55.345 --> 00:01:56.299
Way more.

00:01:56.299 --> 00:01:57.916
I mean look, you might not even be alive.

00:01:57.916 --> 00:02:00.060
Like, your mom and dad could have had sex,

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.733
like three minutes later
and you wouldn't even exist.

00:02:02.733 --> 00:02:04.009
And you're complaining.

00:02:04.009 --> 00:02:06.429
You could've ended up being a bus, a tree.

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:08.444
I just don't get the mentality

00:02:08.444 --> 00:02:11.650
of being head-down sad
on a Monday morning.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.736
I'm going to make Monday morning my bitch.

00:02:13.736 --> 00:02:15.617
I'm going to make you
Saturday, Monday morning.

00:02:15.617 --> 00:02:17.202
That's what I want to do every morning

00:02:17.202 --> 00:02:18.611
and that's what I want from you.

00:02:18.611 --> 00:02:20.405
Please, take a step back

00:02:20.405 --> 00:02:23.546
and think about how
awesome it actually is.

00:02:23.546 --> 00:02:25.875
And then, recognize that
you can attack the world

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:27.586
in a totally different way

00:02:27.586 --> 00:02:28.971
'cause you were lucky enough

00:02:28.971 --> 00:02:31.221
to be born during this era.

00:02:32.174 --> 00:02:33.884
If you're not great at it,

00:02:33.884 --> 00:02:35.565
but you love it more than life,

00:02:35.565 --> 00:02:37.942
should you go after it?

00:02:37.942 --> 00:02:40.025
To me, the answer is yes.

00:02:41.351 --> 00:02:44.060
The problem is, please also recognize

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.912
you're probably not going to get rich.

00:02:46.912 --> 00:02:49.750
Like, if you love
basketball more than life,

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.059
it's just what you've always loved,

00:02:52.059 --> 00:02:56.226
you might just make $49,000 a
year being a basketball coach

00:02:57.244 --> 00:03:00.978
and having a lot of time on
your hand to play basketball.

00:03:00.978 --> 00:03:02.955
It's just, you got to understand,

00:03:02.955 --> 00:03:05.840
you can't have everything
all the time always.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.816
It's just life.

00:03:07.816 --> 00:03:10.118
I think happiness trumps everything.

00:03:10.118 --> 00:03:12.989
Easy for me to say because
it really worked out for me

00:03:12.989 --> 00:03:16.651
'cause happiness coincides
with financial upside.

00:03:16.651 --> 00:03:18.873
I have friends who make $74,000 a year

00:03:18.873 --> 00:03:21.177
that are just happier people than friends

00:03:21.177 --> 00:03:23.679
that are making $18 million
a year that are not.

00:03:23.679 --> 00:03:25.306
You got to do you.

00:03:25.306 --> 00:03:28.463
But please don't let the
entrepreneurial society,

00:03:28.463 --> 00:03:29.296
don't let me,

00:03:29.296 --> 00:03:32.796
don't let your parents push
you into what success is.

00:03:32.796 --> 00:03:34.602
It's different for all of us.

00:03:34.602 --> 00:03:37.526
But, and this is the big but,

00:03:37.526 --> 00:03:40.276
you got to be self aware about it.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.924
Like this is back to self awareness.

00:03:43.924 --> 00:03:45.821
I stay in my lane.

00:03:45.821 --> 00:03:47.531
I'm a salesman, I'm a business builder,

00:03:47.531 --> 00:03:48.971
I've done it my whole life.

00:03:48.971 --> 00:03:51.562
I was an F student at 13-14.

00:03:51.562 --> 00:03:54.713
My friends' parents told my
friends not to hang out with me

00:03:54.713 --> 00:03:56.369
'cause I was a loser.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.249
I'm more successful

00:03:57.249 --> 00:03:59.858
than my entire graduating class combined.

00:03:59.858 --> 00:04:02.694
Like, this is because the
market doesn't understand

00:04:02.694 --> 00:04:03.898
that people don't get it.

00:04:03.898 --> 00:04:06.106
You have to double down on your strengths

00:04:06.106 --> 00:04:07.741
and you have to punt your weaknesses.

00:04:07.741 --> 00:04:10.179
In America, there's
billions of dollars made

00:04:10.179 --> 00:04:11.953
on selling you how to fix the things

00:04:11.953 --> 00:04:13.810
that you're not good at.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.132
It's a huge mistake.

00:04:15.132 --> 00:04:16.783
You need to figure out who you are

00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:18.014
and go all in.

00:04:18.014 --> 00:04:18.929
That's what I did.

00:04:18.929 --> 00:04:21.502
And so when you talk about
business or marketing,

00:04:21.502 --> 00:04:23.095
when you talk about the New York Jets

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:24.582
and when you talk about wine,

00:04:24.582 --> 00:04:26.335
I've got nothing but bravado.

00:04:26.335 --> 00:04:28.602
Everything else, you should see me sitting

00:04:28.602 --> 00:04:30.941
around dinner tables right
now talking about politics.

00:04:30.941 --> 00:04:33.929
The level of humility and
the level of listening

00:04:33.929 --> 00:04:34.981
you wouldn't expect from me

00:04:34.981 --> 00:04:36.818
'cause that's not how
you're used to consuming me.

00:04:36.818 --> 00:04:38.987
I'm loud and proud because
I only stay in my lane.

00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:40.316
Pay very close attention.

00:04:40.316 --> 00:04:42.037
I've got nine years of
content on the internet now,

00:04:42.037 --> 00:04:43.261
maybe a little bit more.

00:04:43.261 --> 00:04:45.934
I've stayed very, very, very narrow.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.517
For me, it's lucky.

00:04:54.847 --> 00:04:56.598
The reason I've been able to kind of grow

00:04:56.598 --> 00:04:58.969
is my narrow thing is consuming behavior,

00:04:58.969 --> 00:05:01.523
which I can deploy against anything.

00:05:01.523 --> 00:05:03.403
So my narrow thing
happens to be quite wide,

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:06.058
which allows me to play, allows
me to be a good investor,

00:05:06.058 --> 00:05:07.389
and allows me to run businesses

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:09.522
and allows me to be a person of (mumbles).

00:05:09.522 --> 00:05:12.023
It allows me to do things.

00:05:12.023 --> 00:05:12.856
- [Interviewer] And it goes

00:05:12.856 --> 00:05:15.157
you barely really think
that failure propels you

00:05:15.157 --> 00:05:17.765
Are there any instances in your past truly

00:05:17.765 --> 00:05:20.347
where you couldn't get over it, and why?

00:05:20.347 --> 00:05:21.180
- Nope.

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:24.488
(audience laughter)

00:05:24.488 --> 00:05:26.940
- And that's why
- By the way,

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.183
By the way, that's the same answer

00:05:29.183 --> 00:05:31.424
for everybody in this room.

00:05:31.424 --> 00:05:33.069
That's what humans are good at.

00:05:33.069 --> 00:05:34.357
We all fail.

00:05:34.357 --> 00:05:35.774
We've all failed.

00:05:36.774 --> 00:05:41.519
Like, my parents haven't
been killed, my child,

00:05:41.519 --> 00:05:43.904
I mean there's people who
have their children die.

00:05:43.904 --> 00:05:45.851
Like, could you imagine?

00:05:45.851 --> 00:05:48.327
Like, the (beep) I deal, listen,

00:05:48.327 --> 00:05:49.802
unfortunately, or fortunately,

00:05:49.802 --> 00:05:51.724
it depends on how one wants to look at it,

00:05:51.724 --> 00:05:52.958
I'm a pretty optimistic guy.

00:05:52.958 --> 00:05:56.644
I lost three of my four
grandparents before I knew them.

00:05:56.644 --> 00:05:59.046
Two before I was born
and one very early on.

00:05:59.046 --> 00:06:02.196
So, it's easy for me to be happy.

00:06:02.196 --> 00:06:05.283
I have my shit in the right order.

00:06:05.283 --> 00:06:07.577
The health and well-being of my family.

00:06:07.577 --> 00:06:11.022
And there's nothing even
remotely close to that.

00:06:11.022 --> 00:06:13.038
Not even remotely.

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:15.433
People have gotten through much worse.

00:06:15.433 --> 00:06:17.384
This is why I'm trying to
recall our grandparents

00:06:17.384 --> 00:06:19.076
and our great-grandparents.

00:06:19.076 --> 00:06:20.912
People were persecuted and killed.

00:06:20.912 --> 00:06:24.151
I just, we do not have real headaches.

00:06:24.151 --> 00:06:28.532
I don't know why I have
this highly emotional

00:06:28.532 --> 00:06:30.791
and then completely
unemotional part of me,

00:06:30.791 --> 00:06:32.988
but I mix them together
to create the balance

00:06:32.988 --> 00:06:33.985
and that's what works for me,

00:06:33.985 --> 00:06:38.046
so of course there's nothing
that I couldn't get up from,

00:06:38.046 --> 00:06:39.970
like every other human ever

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:42.101
besides somebody who now
lives in some weird cave

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:44.227
that we don't know about.

00:06:44.227 --> 00:06:45.190
You know what I mean?

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:46.023
- [Interviewer] I do.

00:06:46.023 --> 00:06:47.221
- We are strong as (beep).

00:06:47.221 --> 00:06:50.111
We're really (beep) strong.

00:06:50.111 --> 00:06:52.119
We're just being sold that we're not.

00:06:52.119 --> 00:06:55.223
'Cause there's a lot of
money, a lot of money

00:06:55.223 --> 00:06:56.954
in telling us that we're not

00:06:56.954 --> 00:06:58.671
pretty enough, thin enough,

00:06:58.671 --> 00:07:01.496
smart enough, good enough.

00:07:01.496 --> 00:07:02.599
(beep) that.

00:07:02.599 --> 00:07:04.293
I want to tell you that
you're the (beep) best.

00:07:04.293 --> 00:07:05.681
Go do (beep).

00:07:05.681 --> 00:07:07.340
We're going to make less money
this year at a hundred million

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.392
than we made last year at sixty-seven.

00:07:09.392 --> 00:07:10.300
Net.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.524
I don't mean percentage.

00:07:11.524 --> 00:07:13.064
Net.

00:07:13.064 --> 00:07:15.790
Meaning, they're in trouble.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:17.139
Them.

00:07:17.139 --> 00:07:18.587
(laughter)

00:07:18.587 --> 00:07:19.829
I see it.

00:07:19.829 --> 00:07:21.819
Which means I over-invested.

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:24.473
More people, more capabilities.

00:07:24.473 --> 00:07:27.908
Because I'm going to take
the whole (beep) pie.

00:07:27.908 --> 00:07:29.565
So, you know what I mean?

00:07:29.565 --> 00:07:31.159
I'm not worried about how much cash

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:33.796
I'm going to take home in 2016

00:07:33.796 --> 00:07:36.531
because I can take a lot more in 2020.

00:07:36.531 --> 00:07:39.816
It's much more fun to take
home 44 million in 2020

00:07:39.816 --> 00:07:43.919
than three million in
2017, 2018, and 2019.

00:07:43.919 --> 00:07:46.304
Instead of four million in 2018.

00:07:46.304 --> 00:07:48.579
People are, ninety-nine percent

00:07:48.579 --> 00:07:50.217
of the market is short-term.

00:07:50.217 --> 00:07:52.591
And the one percent that
isn't and has the talent

00:07:52.591 --> 00:07:54.078
